\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Integrating the fluctuation inside each block}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The [rescaled block mean](fdip-01CJ) separates a hierarchical
Gaussian field into its retained mean and an independent fluctuation
inside each block. A weight such as #{\ue^{-g x^4}} assigns a factor
to each fine site. Taking its conditional expectation therefore
requires the product of these factors inside each block, as in
\ref{fdip-00GI}. What single-site weight does that product give to
the retained field?}
